<title>THAILAND: Reference rate weakens to 32.066-Bank of Thailand.</title>
<headline>Reference rate weakens to 32.066-Bank of Thailand.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Thailand on Friday said the  weighted average interbank exchange rate was 32.066 per dollar against  31.810 on Thursday.</p>
<p>The reference rate is the average rate traded the previous day. It  has been announced daily by the central bank since the July 2 managed  flotation of the baht.</p>
<p>The baht was quoted at 31.85/32.15 to the dollar onshore and 31.80/31.90  in offshore markets early.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
